    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a constrained roster, as key offensive pillars **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** are unavailable due to team off-days. With **Luis Robert Jr.** remaining sidelined on the IL, our offensive output hinges heavily on **Drake Baldwin**, who stands as our strongest play of the day with a score of 57.79. While facing an elite arm in Aaron Nola (3.93 xERA), **Drake Baldwin** earns a significant boost by maintaining the leadoff spot; his ability to maximize plate appearances remains our best path to accumulating counting stats in a low-volume day.\n\nThe secondary slot in our active lineup, occupied by **Dominic Smith**, carries a marginal score of 44.88. His projection is bolstered by a favorable platoon edge, yet this is largely neutralized by his assignment to the nine-hole, which caps his upside for Runs and RBI. Given the shallow depth of today's available roster, **Dominic Smith** was the clear choice to round out the UTIL spot, as other utility options like **Nasim Nunez** or **Sam Antonacci** failed to meet the threshold required to justify utilizing our limited game caps. \n\nRisk management remains a primary focus today. We are navigating a difficult matchup against Nola, which forces us to prioritize floor over ceiling. With **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Curtis Mead**, **Liam Hicks**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, **Franklin Arias**, and **Henry Bolte** all inactive or off-roster, we are effectively playing a defensive game. We advise monitoring pre-game weather reports for any late-developing volatility that could further dampen the offensive environment for **Drake Baldwin** and **Dominic Smith**.",
